        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Almond protein powder is a real, useful protein: defatted almonds, about half protein by weight, with fiber and very little sodium. Bob's Red Mill is the best single-ingredient option and the one to bake with, Wellious is the best shake thanks to its chickpea partner, and Orgain Simple offers the best amino acid balance among blends that include almond.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Just be clear about what it is not. It is not as protein-dense as whey or pea, it is limited in lysine, and it is easy to confuse with almond flour on Amazon. Check the label image, match the size to the price, store it cool, and if anyone in your house has a tree nut allergy, talk to an allergist before it comes through the door.
